story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Warren County came in under 90% of normal in July to August in 35 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same middle ran 52% of normal in July to August and 53% in August to September. So far in 2026 it shows 66% in January to February and 156% in March to April. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 26002 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
